# PROVENANCE: measured, not generated. Every response byte below was captured
# from a genuine DESFire EV1 4K over PC/SC by a PC/SC capture tool
# and is used here as an expectation for our emulator. As with the other
# hardware_genuine_ev1_4k*.vec files, this vector is the opposite of the rest
# of the corpus: the others were recorded from the reference engine, so they
# pin what we decided; this one pins what the silicon does. A mismatch here is
# either a real divergence or a difference we can justify in writing, never a
# vector to be re-recorded from our engine.
#
# Card: UID 045704EA916F80, hardware 1.0, software 1.4, storage 4K. The same
# physical card as hardware_genuine_ev1_4k.vec, formatted and provisioned with
# a synthetic structure whose every key is the all-zero test key. That is what
# makes an authenticated capture safe to commit and replayable: no key material
# enters the tree, and our engine derives the same session key from the same
# pinned nonces.
#
# RndA is the fixed constant the recorder uses; RndB is the card's, recovered
# by decrypting its first authentication frame with the all-zero test key and
# pinned here with inject-random so our engine offers the same challenge.
# What this vector is for: the D40 (0x0A), ISO (0x1A) and AES (0xAA)
# three-pass handshakes, complete, against silicon. Each one is verified
# in both directions by the recorder - the card proves it holds the
# all-zero test key by returning RndA rotated left - so a byte here is a
# measurement of a handshake that actually succeeded, not of one that
# merely produced a plausible-looking frame.

name: genuine EV1 4K, the three authentication handshakes
case-id: hardware-genuine-ev1-4k-handshakes
origin: physical-card
source: captured hardware trace
requires: auth-iso,auth-aes
uid: 045704EA916F80
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-key-len: 16

scan
# The two synthetic applications. KS2 selects the key type: 04 is
# four DES/2K3DES keys, which accepts both the D40 (0x0A) and the ISO
# (0x1A) handshake; 84 is four AES keys, which accepts only 0xAA.
# Both are created without PICC authentication, which PICC key
# settings 0F permit.
status   90CA000005A3A2A10F0400 => 00
status   90CA000005B3B2B10F8400 => 00
#
# D40 (0x0A) on a DES/2K3DES key. Legacy: the reader's token is
# enciphered in the cipher's decrypt direction with an all-zero IV,
# and the card's final frame is verified against RndA rotated left.
status   905A000003A3A2A100 => 00
inject-random CCF53270570A7669
exchange native-apdu 900A0000010000 => DF6AB29AAE46BA2791AF
exchange native-apdu 90AF00001005EEC31F1E6A0CC31FEF8398A662137000 => 26ACED3C771EF9A09100
#
# ISO (0x1A) on the same key. The handshake is ordinary CBC and the
# IV for the second pass is the card's first frame, so the session
# that follows is EV1 rather than D40 even though the key is 2K3DES.
status   905A000003A3A2A100 => 00
inject-random BE0A8CC7458DF222
exchange native-apdu 901A0000010000 => 2D397440D93DF1B291AF
exchange native-apdu 90AF000010A68DDE9E5CC36DA35F88CCF2809D1FD400 => 49FD4910528962FB9100
#
# AES (0xAA), 16-byte blocks throughout.
status   905A000003B3B2B100 => 00
inject-random FE9CB362B535846C37214CC8DFEAE9CE
exchange native-apdu 90AA0000010000 => 98A8C099F438C60DC06BE2CB3E42750891AF
exchange native-apdu 90AF000020FDF466C43944F68391D9DDE54BE910AF9DDB06679C5A28E6343CF550668FE70600 => 0492D1FFBA340E120339490289FF1B079100
#
# A handshake the application's key type does not support.
#
# Each application answers only the handshake its KS2 key type names,
# and both directions of the mismatch were measured. The card refuses
# with 91 AE, an authentication error, and keeps 91 40 for a key number
# beyond the key count, so the two statuses say different things.
#
status   905A000003A3A2A100 => 00
exchange native-apdu 90AA0000010000 => 91AE
status   905A000003B3B2B100 => 00
exchange native-apdu 900A0000010000 => 91AE
exchange native-apdu 901A0000010000 => 91AE
#
# A key number beyond the application's key count, for contrast: this
# is where the card does answer 91 40.
status   905A000003A3A2A100 => 00
exchange native-apdu 900A0000010400 => 9140
